WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.718
IF works in columns, but measures need a little more care.

2
00:00:04.718 --> 00:00:09.704
In this lesson, you will learn to put IF inside a measure, see why

3
00:00:09.704 --> 00:00:14.691
measures need an aggregation like COUNTROWS or SUMX, and read the error messages that

4
00:00:14.691 --> 00:00:17.540
guide you to the fix. Let's debug together!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.866
Here is a measure called Reason.

6
00:00:21.866 --> 00:00:25.154
It checks if there are any cancelled shipments.

7
00:00:25.154 --> 00:00:31.320
Inside IF, CALCULATE with COUNTROWS counts the cancelled rows, and compares the result to zero.

8
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.490
If the count is more than zero, the card says:

9
00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.080
Ask Reason for the Cancelled Shipment. Otherwise: It is okay.

10
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.954
Why not just write Order Status equals Cancelled, like in our column?

11
00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:47.319
Because a measure has no single row.

12
00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:52.049
It looks at many rows at once, so it needs an aggregation to turn

13
00:00:52.049 --> 00:00:53.400
them into one value.

14
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.975
Here I try SUMX instead. The warning appears:

15
00:01:03.975 --> 00:01:07.434
too few arguments were passed to the SUMX function.

16
00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.740
The minimum argument count is two.

17
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.338
SUMX needs a table and an expression.

18
00:01:26.338 --> 00:01:29.820
When one is missing, the visual cannot show a result.

19
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.140
Hover over the warning to read the full message.

20
00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:02.180
It tells you exactly which function needs fixing, and how many arguments it expects.

21
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.272
I check each bracket and each comma.

22
00:02:31.272 --> 00:02:35.000
Many DAX errors come from a bracket in the wrong place.

23
00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.095
Finally, I start again with IF, step by step.

24
00:02:52.095 --> 00:02:57.065
Read the tooltip, add one argument at a time, and test as you go.

25
00:02:57.065 --> 00:02:58.840
That is how professionals debug!

